# Fearless Swashbuckler: "if a Pirate and a Vehicle attacked this combat" is checked again as the ability resolves, and a creature that attacked
# still counts once it has left. On turn three Bot1 attacks with the Swashbuckler and a crewed Air Response Unit; with the trigger on the stack
# Bot2 kills the Swashbuckler with Lightning Bolt (Bot2 has Mox Ruby from its own turn). The Pirate did attack, so the trigger still draws three
# cards (Forest, Mountain, Island, on top of the turn's Island) and discards two (Forest, Mountain). The Vehicle's 3 damage still goes through.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Air Response Unit
Fearless Swashbuckler
Memnite
Island
Forest
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x5
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Air Response Unit.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fearless Swashbuckler.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Air Response Unit.Activate(Ability: Crew)
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Fearless Swashbuckler > Bot2; Air Response Unit > Bot2)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Fearless Swashbuckler)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Fearless Swashbuckler; Black Lotus
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Forest; Mountain)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Mountain; Forest; Fearless Swashbuckler; Black Lotus
